## Clojure -- upstream/clojure/, src/clj/clojure/, test/clj/clojure/, test/clj/derived/

Copyright (c) Rich Hickey and contributors. Distributed under the
Eclipse Public License 1.0, whose text is in epl-v10.html at the root of
this repository and of every release (the file each Clojure source
header names).

- upstream/clojure/ is Clojure's source and test suite, unmodified, from
  github.com/clojure/clojure at the clojure-1.12.6 tag (31a3138a), with
  clojure.spec.alpha 0.5.238 and clojure.core.specs.alpha 0.4.74 from
  their own repositories; the PROVENANCE.md files there say exactly what.
- src/clj/clojure/ and test/clj/clojure/ are MODIFIED copies of those
  files, generated by upstream/derive: each host class name is rewritten
  to clotran's (upstream/class-names.edn). test/clj/derived/ is selected
  from the test suite by upstream/derive-tests. Every file keeps its
  original copyright and license notice, and the modifications are
  distributed under EPL-1.0, as the originals are.
- A release carries these files as source, in lib/clotran/src/clj.

EPL-1.0 and EPL-2.0 are separate licenses. Clojure's files stay under
EPL-1.0 here because that is how they were received; nothing in this
repository relicenses them.

