## Runtime libraries linked into clotran-bin

- GCC's libgfortran, libgcc and (on Linux) libstdc++ are linked
  statically. They are GPLv3 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1,
  which places no conditions on a program built with GCC. libquadmath
  (LGPL) is not linked on macOS or Windows (src/c/quad_stub.c); on Linux
  libgfortran uses the C library's quad-precision routines instead.
- On Windows, the mingw-w64 runtime and winpthreads are linked
  statically. Their notices, which a binary distribution must carry, are
  in packaging/windows/licenses/ and in every Windows release.
